In the afternoon, I go over to Arun's seat.
Arun is the software tester on our team.
I have a question about my work.
"How will my work be checked?" I ask.
He looks at me and smiles.
Arun explains his job clearly.
He shows me a small plan.
"When Maya's work is finished, let me know," he says.
"Then I will check it using this plan."
I look at the plan he prepared.
That plan is very simple.
"How many years has Arun been working as a tester?" I ask.
"I have done this job for three years," he replies.
He has done big projects before this too.
Arun's words put my mind at ease.
I say thank you to him.
After that, I return to my seat.
